.TH "ODIR-UNMOUNT" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-unmount \- unmount: Unmount storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
unmount [storage=<storage>] [sd=<sd>] [<storage\-name>] [drive=<drive>] [device=<device>] [alldrives] [jobid=<jobid>] [job=<job>] [ujobid=<ujobid>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Asks the Storage Daemon to stop using a device and release its volume, so a tape can be removed or the device serviced. While a device is unmounted no job writes to it; mount brings it back. It changes the device state in the Storage Daemon, not the catalog. umount is another name for the same command.
.PP
The storage is given as storage=, sd= or by its bare name; without it a selection list appears. drive= picks one drive, alldrives unmounts every drive of the autochanger one after another. jobid=, job= or ujobid= use the storage of a running job.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "unmount"
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "sd=<sd>"
Storage name (as storage=) (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "<storage\-name>"
Storage name without key (positional value; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "drive=<drive>"
Drive number (number)
.TP
.B "device=<device>"
Device name (text)
.TP
.B "alldrives"
Every drive of the autochanger (keyword)
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>"
Storage of a job (number)
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Storage of a job (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "ujobid=<ujobid>"
Storage of a job (text)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "unmount storage=Autochanger drive=1"
unmount drive 1 of the autochanger
.TP
.B "unmount storage=Autochanger alldrives"
unmount every drive of the autochanger
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
.SH SEE ALSO
